<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Medi-Clinic lifts yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Medi-Clinic lifts yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (millions of rands unless stated)</p>
<p>    Yr shr (cts)	    38.8	   vs  37.2</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)	  7.80	  making 11.55 vs 10.50</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  103.93	  vs  67.94</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  152.12	  vs  97.56</p>
<p>    Tax			 55.12	  vs  34.96</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    8.42	  vs   9.13</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    36.14	  vs  21.77</p>
<p>    Turnover		 981.65	  vs 682.39</p>
<p>Div payable July 31</p>
<p>On register June 27</p>
<p>Full name -  Medi-Clinic Corporation Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said proposed legislation on medical schemes and medicine prices made it difficult to forecast performance over the next year but it was confident that it would be able to maintain its position in the market.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
